 PM MDT, Stream gauges indicate flooding continues for the\nSouth Fork Rio Grande, Rio Grande between South Fork and Del\nNorte, and other area streams.\n- The South Fork Rio Grande and other area streams are past their\ncrests and are continuing to fall. The South Fork Rio Grande is\nexpected to fall back below Flood Stage late Friday night.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDel Norte, South Fork, Wagon Wheel Gap and Creede.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T17:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3049d31a745a79dc4d8679995e0c0fe5a83679c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3049d31a745a79dc4d8679995e0c0fe5a83679c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 7:40AM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Light to moderate rain showers will continue across the southwest\nmountains through the morning, with scattered showers and\npossible thunderstorms, developing across the region through the\nafternoon. Rain, locally heavy associated with the afternoon\nshowers and thunderstorms, will exacerbate ongoing flooding\nissues across the eastern San Juan mountains and Upper Rio Grande\nvalley.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d79